  case                                           with |     with +    
  1. normal enum                                 COMPILES   COMPILES  
  2. codex: ENUMERATOR aliased                   COMPILES   REFUSED   

  the arithmetic, so the result is explicable rather than just observed:
    aliased  -> both FMT and CMD are bit 7, and NBITS collapses 9 -> 8
    with |   -> OR  = 0xff        RHS = (1<<8)-1 = 0xff   EQUAL   -> escapes
    with +   -> SUM = 1+2+4+8+16+32+64+128+128 = 383   RHS = 255  -> caught

=== the OTHER thing codex found: 1u << NBITS at NBITS == 32 ===
    /tmp/enumalias/w.c: In function 'main':
    /tmp/enumalias/w.c:1:35: warning: left shift count >= width of type [-Wshift-count-overflow]
        1 | int main(void) { unsigned x = (1u << 32) - 1u; return (int)x; }
    (a diagnostic above = it fails LOUDLY rather than silently miscomputing)

ENUMALIAS_DONE
